<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-ABARE details Australia winter plantings.</title>
<headline>RTRS-ABARE details Australia winter plantings.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Bureau of Agricultural and Resource Economics (ABARE) reported the following planting details for Australia's winter crops (July/June), in thousand hectares (ha).</p>
<p>			1996/97    1997/98     Change</p>
<p>			estimate   forecast    percent</p>
<p>    CEREALS	  15,469     14,811	-4.3</p>
<p>    Wheat	    11,002     10,501	-4.6</p>
<p>    Barley	    3,258	3,189	-2.1</p>
<p>    Oats		  908	  917	+1.0</p>
<p>    Triticale	   301	  204     -32.2</p>
<p>    PULSES	    1,904	1,927	+1.2</p>
<p>    Chickpeas	   223	  217	-2.7</p>
<p>    Faba beans	   90	   89	 0.0</p>
<p>    Field peas	  305	  262     -14.1</p>
<p>    Lentils		18	   40    +122.2</p>
<p>    Lupins	    1,226	1,280	+4.4</p>
<p>    Mung beans	   42	   39	-7.1</p>
<p>    OIL SEEDS	   414	  610     +47.3</p>
<p>    Canola		375	  565     +50.6</p>
<p>    Linseed		 8	    8	 0.0</p>
<p>    Safflower	    31	   37     +19.4</p>
<p>    TOTAL	    17,790     17,348	-2.5</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
